title: Confronting the Trump Movement
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: confronting_trump_timer <= 0 and maga_strength >= 25
on-arrival: confronting_trump_timer = 8

= Confronting the Trump Movement

A populist, nationalist movement is reshaping the Republican Party and challenging democratic norms. How do we respond?

- @expose_threat: Sound the alarm
- @address_grievances: Address the grievances behind the movement
- @build_cross_party: Build a cross-party defense of democracy
- @mock_it: Mock and ignore
- @easy_discard

@expose_threat
subtitle: raises urgency
on-arrival: trump_urgency += 1.5; pro_democracy += 1; polarization += 1; maga_strength -= 1; dem_enthusiasm += 0.5; gopmod_relation -= 2; month_actions += 1

We warn that democratic norms are under threat. The base is energized, though some say we cry wolf.

@address_grievances
on-arrival: maga_strength -= 3; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); rural_dem += 3*(1-dissent); populist_strength += 2; progressive_dissent += 3; polarization -= 1; month_actions += 1

We talk honestly about trade, towns left behind, and distrust of elites, and offer real alternatives.

@build_cross_party
on-arrival: gopmod_relation += 6; maga_strength -= 1.5; institutions += 2; progressive_dissent += 2; trump_urgency += 0.8; pro_democracy += 1.5; month_actions += 1

Never-Trump Republicans, civil libertarians, and business leaders join us in a coalition that tolerates uneasy bedfellows.

@mock_it
on-arrival: trump_urgency -= 0.5; polarization += 1.5; maga_strength += 2; gop_enthusiasm += 0.5; suburban_dem += 1*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

Satire lands well with our base but also galvanizes our opponents. Ignoring the movement is not working.
